---Note that there may be a 5-second end-point resolution issue. For instance, if a cuepoint comes in for 22:03:27, we may stuff the cuepoint into 22:03:25 or 22:03:30, depending. This is an artifact of HLS.
---@class gcp.youtube_v3.Cuepoint
---@field cueType? gcp.youtube_v3.CuepointCueTypeEnum
---@field id? string The identifier for cuepoint resource.
---@field etag? string
---@field durationSecs? number The duration of this cuepoint.
---@field insertionOffsetTimeMs? string The time when the cuepoint should be inserted by offset to the broadcast actual start time.
---@field walltimeMs? string The wall clock time at which the cuepoint should be inserted. Only one of insertion_offset_time_ms and walltime_ms may be set at a time.

---@alias gcp.youtube_v3.CuepointCueTypeEnum "cueTypeUnspecified"|"cueTypeAd"

---Schedule to insert cuepoints into a broadcast by ads automator.
---@class gcp.youtube_v3.CuepointSchedule
---@field scheduleStrategy? gcp.youtube_v3.CuepointScheduleScheduleStrategyEnum|string The strategy to use when scheduling cuepoints.
---@field pauseAdsUntil? string If set, automatic cuepoint insertion is paused until this timestamp ("No Ad Zone"). The value is specified in ISO 8601 format.
---@field repeatIntervalSecs? number Interval frequency in seconds that api uses to insert cuepoints automatically.
---@field enabled? boolean This field is semantically required. If it is set false or not set, other fields in this message will be ignored.

---@alias gcp.youtube_v3.CuepointScheduleScheduleStrategyEnum "scheduleStrategyUnspecified"|"concurrent"|"nonConcurrent"

