---Basic broadcast information.
---@class gcp.youtube_v3.LiveBroadcastSnippet
---@field categoryId? string The YouTube [video category](https://developers.google.com/youtube/data/reference/rest/v3/videoCategories/list) associated with the video broadcast.
---@field title? string The broadcast's title. Note that the broadcast represents exactly one YouTube video. You can set this field by modifying the broadcast resource or by setting the [`title`](https://developers.google.com/youtube/data/reference/rest/v3/videos#snippet.title) field of the corresponding video resource.
---@field liveChatId? string The id of the live chat for this broadcast.
---@field scheduledStartTime? string The date and time that the broadcast is scheduled to start.
---@field thumbnails? gcp.youtube_v3.ThumbnailDetails A map of thumbnail images associated with the broadcast. For each nested object in this object, the key is the name of the thumbnail image, and the value is an object that contains other information about the thumbnail.
---@field actualEndTime? string The date and time that the broadcast actually ended. This information is only available once the broadcast's state is complete.
---@field channelId? string The ID that YouTube uses to uniquely identify the channel that is publishing the broadcast.
---@field actualStartTime? string The date and time that the broadcast actually started. This information is only available once the broadcast's state is live.
---@field publishedAt? string The date and time that the broadcast was added to YouTube's live broadcast schedule.
---@field description? string The broadcast's description. As with the title, you can set this field by modifying the broadcast resource or by setting the [`description`](https://developers.google.com/youtube/data/reference/rest/v3/videos#snippet.description) field of the corresponding video resource.
---@field scheduledEndTime? string The date and time that the broadcast is scheduled to end.
---@field isDefaultBroadcast? boolean Indicates whether this broadcast is the default broadcast. Internal only.

---Statistics about the live broadcast. These represent a snapshot of the values at the time of the request. Statistics are only returned for live broadcasts.
---@class gcp.youtube_v3.LiveBroadcastStatistics
---@field concurrentViewers? string The number of viewers currently watching the broadcast. The property and its value will be present if the broadcast has current viewers and the broadcast owner has not hidden the viewcount for the video. Note that YouTube stops tracking the number of concurrent viewers for a broadcast when the broadcast ends. So, this property would not identify the number of viewers watching an archived video of a live broadcast that already ended.

