---Freebase topic information related to the video.
---@class gcp.youtube_v3.VideoTopicDetails
---@field relevantTopicIds? gcp.youtube_v3.StringList Similar to topic_id, except that these topics are merely relevant to the video. These are topics that may be mentioned in, or appear in the video. You can retrieve information about each topic using Freebase Topic API.
---@field topicCategories? gcp.youtube_v3.StringList A list of Wikipedia URLs that provide a high-level description of the video's content.
---@field topicIds? gcp.youtube_v3.StringList A list of Freebase topic IDs that are centrally associated with the video. These are topics that are centrally featured in the video, and it can be said that the video is mainly about each of these. You can retrieve information about each topic using the < a href="http://wiki.freebase.com/wiki/Topic_API">Freebase Topic API.

---Specifies who is allowed to train on the video.
---@class gcp.youtube_v3.VideoTrainability
---@field videoId? string The ID of the video.
---@field kind? string Identifies what kind of resource this is. Value: the fixed string "youtube#videoTrainability".
---@field etag? string Etag of this resource.
---@field permitted? gcp.youtube_v3.StringList Specifies who is allowed to train on the video. Valid values are: - a single string "all" - a single string "none" - a list of allowed parties

---Branding properties for the watch. All deprecated.
---@class gcp.youtube_v3.WatchSettings
---@field backgroundColor? string The text color for the video watch page's branded area.
---@field featuredPlaylistId? string An ID that uniquely identifies a playlist that displays next to the video player.
---@field textColor? string The background color for the video watch page's branded area.

